# Third-party reference documents -- NOT ignored for clutter.
# reference/official_H3_references/ is MiniMax's published prompting guides verbatim, and the
# ELIF summary is a community author's writing. This remote is PUBLIC, and git history keeps a
# file even after it is deleted, so committing them is a redistribution decision rather than a
# housekeeping one. Held deliberately until that call is made; delete these two lines to publish.
reference/official_H3_references/
reference/unofficial_ELIF_summary_of_H3_references/

# Experiment artifacts that are duplicates or regenerable.
#
# run_tests.py writes each round TWICE: one concatenated <family>__<tag>.txt, plus a directory
# of per-case files beside it. The concatenated file is what validate.py, score.py and every
# collect script actually read, so it is the evidence and it is TRACKED. The per-case directories
# hold the same text again -- 1,221 files and 5MB across the two bloat rounds -- and are not.
# (See also L-STALE-PER-CASE-FILES: those directories are a mixture of rounds, not a snapshot of
# one, so they are actively misleading to read from.)
reference/experiments/*/runs/*/

# Derived from the run files by collect2.py on demand.
reference/experiments/*/runs/_split/

# Tokenizer cache. Keyed on the exact text, so it cannot go stale silently -- and it rebuilds
# from the live tokenizer, which is where the numbers have to come from anyway.
**/.tokcache.json

# Python build artifacts
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
